#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119623 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119812 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3c3466c-dfb0-5b5f-b556-ce57a1d78519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether a Vector Lies in the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "fe2f3934-fa5c-5a59-be7e-00b6e4889063" :question/math-academy-id "e-4810" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and vectors $\\mathbf{b}_1$, $\\mathbf{b}_2$, $\\mathbf{b}_3$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\textrm{Null}(A)?$\n\n![](images/98/9832b17728be69381a5f534317c0f30156fd32f3706f4cd4634765a02370180e.png)" :question/worked-solution "A vector $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Null}(A)$ if $A\\mathbf{b}=\\mathbf{0}.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $\\mathbf{0}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 16\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-27 \\\\ 45 \\\\ 72\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 16\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0\\,✓ \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 16\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ 25 \\\\ 40\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $\\mathbf{b}_2$ lies in $\\textrm{Null}(A).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119624 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9171c6fb-ad0b-538f-b982-a2502a20e253" :knowledge-point/title "Solve a Variable in a Vector Lying in the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "e38db5fa-1753-5176-bb5e-a077ea63ddec" :question/math-academy-id "e-4812" :question/problem "Consider the matrix ![](images/a8/a8b13d238a1e77d90abe70a505c68a72060ea95fe545f56ae53e7cf40ba0595e.png) and the vector ![](images/6e/6e9f6c010c3137438923dfc32674dedf6d2d554b9b0a6745b007d826954d1e65.png) Find the value of $k$ such that $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\textrm{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Null}(A),$ then we must have $A\\mathbf{b} = \\mathbf{0}.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 6 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ k \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}6+2k-12 \\\\ -6+3k-3 \\\\ 12-6k+6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2k-6=0 \\\\ 3k-9=0 \\\\ -6k+18=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119625 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "465ce2b7-352e-5050-a5e4-0753fbacebf5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "1e59cd29-ea54-5b90-8215-60c81d1b6dbb" :question/math-academy-id "e-4814" :question/problem "Consider the matrix ![](images/78/787a2e53b8e39e79e0e4a2379082187a445a9c6babe0677fa315c516c01f0f67.png) Find $\\textrm{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -12 \\\\ 3 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second equation tells us that $x_2=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-3(0) & =0 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that ![](images/f7/f73d7951a041c633d78d1d6971a3473800727452bb92e1b39ad574a045e1b76f.png) is the only solution to this system.\n\nTherefore, $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\left\\{ \\mathbf{0} \\right\\}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402362 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119812 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3c3466c-dfb0-5b5f-b556-ce57a1d78519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether a Vector Lies in the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0957d54-3a75-5c9c-85ed-c3fc9e27319a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402364} {:answer/id #uuid "a07d906a-9817-56bc-a8bc-f84fb817ea22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402365} {:answer/id #uuid "ffba3c8a-b1b6-5ff8-95f5-61453383f036" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402366} {:answer/id #uuid "574e668b-516f-527f-a863-a5d86ad524ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{2}$ and ${b}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402367} {:answer/id #uuid "6b7c7a5a-0d78-5275-8321-8300ff247f49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0957d54-3a75-5c9c-85ed-c3fc9e27319a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402364} :answer-field/id #uuid "504c5c81-a875-5c21-b5d2-42ca7fdd3f22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402363}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cade4505-b877-5cb5-ae1c-bc1354365d4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-34361" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and vectors ${b}_{1}$, ${b}_{2}$, ${b}_{3}$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\text{Null}(A)?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -10 & 8\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A)$ if $Ab=0.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -10 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}41 \\\\ 82\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -10 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0\\,✓ \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -10 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only ${b}_{2}$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A).$"}]}
